{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/603019-obfuscated-and-blood-sympathy","id":603019,"title":"Obfuscated and Blood Sympathy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-25T09:49:55-07:00","id":603019,"title":"Obfuscated and Blood Sympathy","content":"Hey, fairly new here.<br /> <br /> The rules are pretty clear about how Auspex interacts with Obfuscate but I couldn't find anything about this.<br /> <br /> Two scenarios in mind:<br /> <br /> 1) A Kindred with Obfuscate 3 is hiding from their Sire. Would activating Obfuscate 1 or 3 hinder their Sire's ability to use Blood Sympathy to detect their presence?<br /> <br /> 2) a Kindred is trapped in a building concealed by Obfuscate 5. Would any of their relatives be able to get any kind of Blood Sympathy from them without using Auspex to pierce the Obfuscate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7033-funsize","name":"FunSize","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T10:07:23-07:00","id":603050,"title":"","content":"Well, Blood Sympathy only tells you the relative's mental state and general direction (and distance on an exceptional success). Obfuscate wouldn't prevent it, but that information wouldn't really help you find an obfuscated vampire. In example 1, the sire might know that her childe is in the same room and somewhere to the left, but that doesn't allow her to actually see him if he's hidden with Obfuscate 3. In example 2, a relative could use Blood Sympathy to know that the kindred is in distress, and roughly the direction and distance to the building, but they wouldn't be able to actually find the building unless they had some other means of breaking the Obfuscate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T15:24:43-07:00","id":603246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FunSize</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/603019-obfuscated-and-blood-sympathy#post603019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, fairly new here.<br /> <br /> The rules are pretty clear about how Auspex interacts with Obfuscate but I couldn't find anything about this.<br /> <br /> Two scenarios in mind:<br /> <br /> 1) A Kindred with Obfuscate 3 is hiding from their Sire. Would activating Obfuscate 1 or 3 hinder their Sire's ability to use Blood Sympathy to detect their presence?<br /> <br /> 2) a Kindred is trapped in a building concealed by Obfuscate 5. Would any of their relatives be able to get any kind of Blood Sympathy from them without using Auspex to pierce the Obfuscate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Treat as a clash of wills. If so desire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T17:15:10-07:00","id":603316,"title":"","content":"I go with Charlaquin. There are no reason to think Obfuscate should hinder Blood Sympathy, but it wouldn't also do anything to surpass Obfuscate. They don't clash because they don't really interact rules-wise, what one prevents isn't what the other gets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T04:16:43-07:00","id":603734,"title":"","content":"Blood Sympathy is described as a mystical perception and communication ability, costs willpower to use and has a much further range of use for detection even for those with the furthest ties, there is absolutely no reason to say it doesn't have the potential to pierce through Obfuscate. So yes, if you abduct someone and hide them away in your magically hidden fortress, you may be providing their blood relative the impetus to provoke a clash of wills to see your hidden building they would not have had otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T07:01:13-07:00","id":603793,"title":"","content":"I'd categorize Blood Sympathy as a sense. Per the sidebar in the Obfuscate section, it should affect Blood Sympathy as easily as someone's eyes. There is an argument for it creating a Clash of Wills, though I'm not sure what the dicepool would be. Probably Blood Potency + Blood Sympathy Bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T09:51:25-07:00","id":603907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/603019-obfuscated-and-blood-sympathy?p=603734#post603734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood Sympathy is described as a mystical perception and communication ability, costs willpower to use and has a much further range of use for detection even for those with the furthest ties, there is absolutely no reason to say it doesn't have the potential to pierce through Obfuscate. So yes, if you abduct someone and hide them away in your magically hidden fortress, you may be providing their blood relative the impetus to provoke a clash of wills to see your hidden building they would not have had otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the relative's specific location isn't information that Blood Sympathy gives you in the first place. If they're trapped in a building that <i>isn't</i> obfuscated you don't get to know exactly where it is, just the general direction (and if you get an exceptional success, the rough distance). You don't even get to know that they're in a building, just that they're in distress and they're about 5 miles thataway. It wouldn't make a whole lot of sense for Blood Sympathy to give you <i>more</i> information if the relative is obfuscated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-26-2015, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T13:47:50-07:00","id":604068,"title":"","content":"Yeah,, you could argue that Obfuscate obscures Blood Sympathy (calling for a Clash of Wills), but in no way that B-S can break the Obfuscate effect.<br /> <br /> For that you have Aupex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T04:08:57-07:00","id":604585,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt; But the relative's specific location isn't information that Blood Sympathy gives you in the first place... You don't even get to know that they're in a building, just that they're in distress and they're about 5 miles thataway. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> It's specific enough so that if the searcher goes 5 miles thataway, finds a vacant lot, or does a cursory search through the recreation of the Worlds Fair Hotel or whatever disguised effect of obfuscate, make another sympathy check which tells them their kin should be right there, lash out on their kin and shatter <u>every</u> obfuscate effect on him.<br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; you could argue that Obfuscate obscures Blood Sympathy (calling for a Clash of Wills) &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> And my response would be, Obfuscate doesn't conceal one's blood ties to their predecessors, offspring, or clanmates. It's also a moot point involving relatives, you get a bonus to use powers hide yourself, they get the exact same bonus to use powers to find you.<br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; but in no way that B-S can break the Obfuscate effect. <br /> For that you have Aupex. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> All one needs to individually see through obfuscate is to interact with the obfuscated object or person or the ability to overcome the obfuscate user's rating as a penalty on a perception roll. If one wants to dispel it entirely, they can simply lash out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T09:47:42-07:00","id":604774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/603019-obfuscated-and-blood-sympathy?p=604585#post604585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's specific enough so that if the searcher goes 5 miles thataway, finds a vacant lot, or does a cursory search through the recreation of the Worlds Fair Hotel or whatever disguised effect of obfuscate, make another sympathy check which tells them their kin should be right there, lash out on their kin and shatter <u>every</u> obfuscate effect on him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. But that's the Lash Out that breaks thr obfuscate, not the Blood Sympathy. Blood Sympathy is a useful tool that could help you narrow down where to look for an obfuscated relative, but it doesn't break obfuscate by itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T10:10:21-07:00","id":604789,"title":"","content":"I'm getting this daft image of a vampire running back and forth in an attempt to triangulate the obfuscated vamp's position now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T10:31:33-07:00","id":604802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/603019-obfuscated-and-blood-sympathy?p=604789#post604789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm getting this daft image of a vampire running back and forth in an attempt to triangulate the obfuscated vamp's position now.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Marco!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Polo!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T01:57:00-07:00","id":605417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/603019-obfuscated-and-blood-sympathy?p=604802#post604802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Marco!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Polo!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Age of Vampires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T10:38:38-07:00","id":606833,"title":"","content":"I quite like the image of a vampire reaching out with an inhuman sense, trying to feel past the veil of obfuscate. Either fevered searching or measured and calm. Imagine the tension for anybody under the obfuscate, looking out and seeing the kindred searching for them, so close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T05:41:43-07:00","id":609284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenagain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/603019-obfuscated-and-blood-sympathy?p=606833#post606833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I quite like the image of a vampire reaching out with an inhuman sense, trying to feel past the veil of obfuscate. Either fevered searching or measured and calm. Imagine the tension for anybody under the obfuscate, looking out and seeing the kindred searching for them, so close.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's great imagery...calling out to the Blood, hearing the Blood call back in terror, and the helplessness of not knowing where it's calling from or how to find it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7033-funsize","name":"FunSize","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}